+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the providers so the model knows how to shape its calls, but nothing checked what the model actually sent: an executor received whatever arrived, and each tool defended itself in its own way -- or not at all. Validation therefore lives in `ToolRegistry` itself, once, using the same schema handed to the providers (compiled with `ajv`), so there is no second schema format to drift and no opt-out. A call the schema rejects becomes a tool result the model can read and correct within the existing tool-round budget; it never ends the conversation as a generic transport error.
+
+## The contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the resolved definition's `inputSchema` before the executor runs; a call missing a required property is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names that property as required, and the executor is never invoked
+  ([validated by: rejects a call missing a required property and leaves the executor uninvoked](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- Valid input carrying a property the schema does not declare reaches the executor unchanged and exactly once -- validation injects no defaults, coerces nothing, and rejects nothing on undeclared keys
+  ([validated by: passes an unlisted extra property through to the executor unchanged and exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L51)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected with a message naming the field's path and the expected type, and that message carries no property value
+  ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming the path and expected type, carrying no value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L64)).
+- A value violating a declared `enum` is rejected, and the rejection names the property that failed
+  ([validated by: rejects a value violating a declared enum and names the property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L81)).
+- Neither a rejection's returned text nor any log line the registry writes carries a property value from the rejected input; tool input is where identifying data enters the engine, and the engine redacts nothing downstream of it
+  ([validated by: rejects input without naming the offending value in the result or any log line](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L104)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled once, at `register` time -- ten `execute` calls against it invoke the schema compiler exactly once
+  ([validated by: compiles a static schema once across ten execute calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L128)).
+- An uncompilable schema fails at `register` with an error naming the tool, so a broken schema surfaces at startup rather than mid-conversation
+  ([validated by: throws at register naming the tool when the schema cannot compile](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L143)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call, and each call is validated against the schema current at that call
+  ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L154)).
+- `execute` throws `Unknown tool: <name>` for an unregistered name, unchanged by validation -- the throw is the one failure class left to the caller
+  ([validated by: throws an Unknown tool error for an unregistered name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L183)).
+- A rejected tool call travels back to the provider as a tool result: the orchestrator's `processMessage` resolves rather than rejecting, and the provider sees the rejection text on the next round, where a corrected call succeeds within the existing tool-round budget
+  ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider and resolves on the corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L50)).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Validating tool _output_; the schema governs what the model sends, not what a tool returns.
+- Hallucination detection and an evaluation harness.
+- Per-tool authorization: a schema-valid call for someone else's data is still valid, and authorization is a `ToolContext` boundary concern (_Let a consumer decline a tool call through a `beforeToolCall` hook_ is a veto seam, not an authorization model).
+- Retry, timeout and rate limiting around tool execution.
+- Returning an unknown tool name to the model instead of throwing; the throw is kept as-is on purpose and tracked as its own issue.
